{"total_count":378,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36770","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36770/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36770/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36770/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36770","id":5205616483,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABAcWibg","number":36770,"title":"feat(API): Add git connections pull to import projects from working copy (no-changelog)","user":{"login":"ireneea","id":20843309,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODQzMzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20843309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea","html_url":"https://github.com/ireneea","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1417801469,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE3ODAxNDY5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/node/improvement","name":"node/improvement","color":"008672","default":false,"description":"New feature or request"},{"id":1417801476,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE3ODAxNDc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/core","name":"core","color":"DC143C","default":false,"description":"Enhancement outside /nodes-base and /editor-ui"},{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-08-20T16:23:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T16:05:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/36770","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36770","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36770.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36770.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds a pull that imports every project from a git connection's local working copy (`repository/n8n-export`) into the instance, overwriting to match the on-disk package. Git fetch/clone stays out of scope, so it imports whatever the last clone produced.\n\n- `DirectoryPackageReader`: a filesystem `PackageReader` over the unzipped package, reusing the import size/path guards; `importPackage` is refactored to dispatch on a pre-built reader, plus a new `importPackageFromDirectory` (empty manifest = no-op).\n- `GitConnectionsService.pull` with a fixed source-of-truth overwrite policy, returning `GitConnectionPullResultDto` (per-status counts).\n- New public API `POST /git-connections/:id/pull` gated by `gitConnection:pull`, and a `git-connections pull` CLI command.\n\n## How to test\n\n1. Configure a git connection so a working copy exists at `repository/n8n-export`.\n2. Call `POST /git-connections/:id/pull` (or run the `git-connections pull` CLI command) and confirm projects are imported/overwritten and the per-status counts are returned.\n3. See `import-project-from-directory.integration.test.ts` and the added unit/integration tests for coverage.\n\n## Related Linear tickets, Github issues, and Community forum posts\n\nhttps://linear.app/n8n/issue/LIGO-968\n\n## Review / Merge checklist\n\n- [x] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\n- [x] PR title and summary are descriptive. ([conventions](../blob/master/.github/pull_request_title_conventions.md))\n- [ ] [Docs updated](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs) or follow-up ticket created.\n- [x] Tests included.\n- [x] PR Labeled with `Backport to Beta`, `Backport to Stable`, or `Backport to v1` (if the PR is an urgent fix that needs to be backported)\n\n🤖 PR Summary generated by AI\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36770?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36770/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36770/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36120","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36120/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36120/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36120/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36120","id":5129641629,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs79_Kr8","number":36120,"title":"feat(core): Add n8n-test workflow-testing PoC (no-changelog)","user":{"login":"geemanjs","id":1285296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODUyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1285296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs","html_url":"https://github.com/geemanjs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geemanjs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-12T10:01:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T13:29:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/36120","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36120","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36120.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36120.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"> [!WARNING]\n> **Spike — do not merge.** Throwaway proof of concept for a demo; it lives on this branch only.\n\n## Summary\n\nProves an n8n workflow (`workflow.json`) can be tested like code: `packages/n8n-test` exposes `await runWorkflow(workflowJson, input?)`, which executes the workflow through the **real n8n engine** (real `WorkflowExecute`, real `nodes-base` node implementations) inside a vitest test, with HTTP intercepted by nock.\n\n**Version 2** (branch `ligo-workflow-testing-v2`) adds:\n\n- **`mockNode(workflowJson, nodeName, cannedOutput)`** — swap any number of named nodes for canned results while everything else runs real; the returned handle captures what the node received (`sub.input()`). Star demo: mocking an Execute Sub-workflow node, which cannot run under the harness — asserted in both directions.\n- **The CI story, for real.** `pnpm --filter n8n-test bundle` produces a self-contained tarball (vendored `core/nodes-testing` loaders, `../dist` imports rewritten to `n8n-core/dist` deep requires) that runs on **released npm** n8n packages. The demo repo [geemanjs/n8n-workflow-testing-demo](https://github.com/geemanjs/n8n-workflow-testing-demo) holds an exploded project package export; [PR #1](https://github.com/geemanjs/n8n-workflow-testing-demo/pull/1) there shows a workflow-breaking change failing CI in ~65s with a readable assertion diff.\n\nFeasibility was adversarially verified both rounds: tampering expressions changes outputs, the HTTP node's genuine request path is what nock intercepts, and unmocked nodes around a mock still execute for real.\n\nThe gotchas the real feature must own are in [`packages/n8n-test/README.md`](../blob/ligo-workflow-testing-v2/packages/n8n-test/README.md) — headline items: mock-`additionalData` hazards, trigger semantics per execution mode, released-engine drift (version pins, DI dedupe, node `typeVersion` availability), and Code-node/sub-workflow capabilities needing `mockNode`.\n\nSpecs and plans are committed on the branches: `.agents/specs/n8n-test-poc.md` (v1), `.agents/specs/n8n-test-poc-v2.md` (v2).\n\n## How to test\n\n```bash\ngit fetch && git checkout ligo-workflow-testing-v2\npnpm exec turbo run build --filter=n8n-core --filter=n8n-nodes-base   # one-off: nodes load from built dist\npnpm --filter n8n-test demo                                           # 7 tests through the real engine\n```\n\nOr entirely outside the monorepo: clone the [demo repo](https://github.com/geemanjs/n8n-workflow-testing-demo), `npm install && npm test`.\n\n## Related Linear tickets, Github issues, and Community forum posts\n\nNone — engineering spike ahead of a product pitch.\n\n## Review / Merge checklist\n\n- [ ] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\n- [ ] PR title and summary are descriptive. ([conventions](../blob/master/.github/pull_request_title_conventions.md))\n- [ ] [Docs updated](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs) or follow-up ticket created.\n- [ ] Tests included.\n- [ ] PR Labeled with `Backport to Beta`, `Backport to Stable`, or `Backport to v1` (if the PR is an urgent fix that needs to be backported)\n\n🤖 PR Summary generated by AI","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36120/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36120/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36746","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36746/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36746/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36746/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36746","id":5204380867,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABAbV7Ng","number":36746,"title":"test: Pin the diff parsing and source filter in mutate.mjs","user":{"login":"shortstacked","id":7861842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NjE4NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7861842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked","html_url":"https://github.com/shortstacked","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shortstacked/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1417801476,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE3ODAxNDc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/core","name":"core","color":"DC143C","default":false,"description":"Enhancement outside /nodes-base and /editor-ui"},{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-08-20T14:16:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T11:35:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/36746","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36746","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36746.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36746.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"conveyor:test-assist\n\n## Summary\n\nChecked whether the tests covering this patch catch changes to it. **6 changed lines were not pinned by any assertion — strengthened 6.** Test files only; no product source touched.\n\n**Scope note (important):** `pnpm mutate --diff` printed `Nothing mutable changed vs origin/master` and exited 0. That is *not* a green. This PR's only source change is `scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs`, and the tool skips it twice over — `isMutableSource` accepts `.ts`/`.tsx` only, and the runner is vitest while these tests are `node:test`. I scored the changed lines directly with Stryker's **command** runner instead (throwaway config, deleted; repro below).\n\n| Scope | Before | After | Left |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `mutate.mjs` exported helpers (changed lines) | 83.19% | **88.24%** | 14 |\n| `mutate.mjs` all changed lines | 18.43% | 19.82% | 348 |\n\n### Strengthened\n\n- `scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs:318` — a hunk header's line count may run past one digit on either side; `@@ -80,12 +90,14 @@` must yield `90-103` rather than being dropped. Every existing case used a single-digit count, so any hunk of 10+ lines — most of them — could have been silently skipped by `--diff` with no test noticing.\n- `scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs:318` — only a header at the *start* of a line is a header; `@@ …` text inside a `+`/`-` content line is not. (Reachable here: a `git diff` of any file that itself contains hunk-header strings, such as `mutate.test.mjs`.)\n- `scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs:297` — the extension test is anchored: a path merely *containing* `.ts` — a committed `foo.test.ts.snap` sitting beside its source — is not mutable TypeScript.\n- `scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs:297` / `:284` — `.mts`/`.cts` are accepted as source, and `.test.mts` is excluded as a test. The `[cm]?` class was unpinned on both sides.\n\nAll four are plain example cases added to the tests that already covered those lines; one new `it` was added for the `^`-anchor rule, which no existing case exercised.\n\n### Left alone\n\n- `mutate.mjs:280` (`BLOCKED_PACKAGES`) — the guard that keeps Stryker off the isolated-vm package. Neither it nor `ineligibleReason` is exported, so pinning it needs a product-source change, which is out of scope for this pass. This is the highest-value survivor remaining and worth a follow-up.\n- `mutate.mjs:336` — dropping `^` from `/^(.*):(\\d+)-(\\d+)$/` is **equivalent**: a leading greedy `.*` already makes the anchor redundant. Dropping `$` needs a malformed target like `src/a.ts:1-2x`, not reachable from real CLI usage.\n- `mutate.mjs:283-290` (`NON_SOURCE` anchors) — the `^` alternatives only fire for a repo-root-level `dist/`, `test/`, `migrations/` or `__tests__/` directory, none of which exist in this repo.\n- `mutate.mjs:340-749` — 334 survivors across `planFromDiff`, `runJob`, `reportJob`, `main` and the git/fs helpers. None of that layer is exported or unit-tested at all; it is what drags the all-changed-lines figure down to 19.82%. Closing it needs a process-level harness, not an assertion tweak.\n\n## How to test\n\n```bash\nnode --test --experimental-test-module-mocks scripts/mutation-health/mutate.test.mjs\n```\n\nTo reproduce the mutation scoring (the packaged `pnpm mutate` cannot target this file):\n\n```js\n// /tmp/stryker.selfcheck.mjs\nexport default {\n  testRunner: 'command',\n  commandRunner: {\n    command: 'node --test --experimental-test-module-mocks scripts/mutation-health/mutate.test.mjs',\n  },\n  reporters: ['progress', 'json'],\n  coverageAnalysis: 'off',\n  mutate: [],\n  jsonReporter: { fileName: '.selfcheck/raw.json' },\n  concurrency: 1,\n};\n```\n\n```bash\nnode node_modules/@stryker-mutator/core/bin/stryker.js run /tmp/stryker.selfcheck.mjs \\\n  --inPlace --mutate \"scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs:104-131,scripts/mutation-health/mutate.mjs:277-338\"\n```\n\n<details><summary>Detail — the changes no test caught</summary>\n\n| Location | Mutator | Undetected change | Covering test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `mutate.mjs:318` | Regex | `(?:,(\\d+))?` → `(?:,(\\d))?` (new-side count) | `parseHunkRanges > reads new-side ranges out of \\`git diff -U0\\` headers` |\n| `mutate.mjs:318` | Regex | `(?:,\\d+)?` → `(?:,\\d)?` (old-side count) | same |\n| `mutate.mjs:318` | Regex | `/^@@ …/` → `/@@ …/` | same |\n| `mutate.mjs:297` | Regex | `/\\.[cm]?tsx?$/` → `/\\.[cm]?tsx?/` | `isMutableSource > rejects tests, declarations, configs and build output` |\n| `mutate.mjs:297` | Regex | `/\\.[cm]?tsx?$/` → `/\\.[^cm]?tsx?$/` | `isMutableSource > accepts product source wherever a package keeps it` |\n| `mutate.mjs:284` | Regex | `/\\.(test\\|spec)\\.[cm]?tsx?$/` → `/\\.(test\\|spec)\\.[^cm]?tsx?$/` | `isMutableSource > rejects tests, declarations, configs and build output` |\n\n`classifyRun` (also new on this branch) had **no** survivors — its six existing cases already pin it fully.\n\n</details>\n\n## Verification\n\n| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `pnpm mutate --diff` | exit 0, `Nothing mutable changed vs origin/master` — see scope note; this patch is invisible to the tool's own filter |\n| `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --dir ./.github/scripts --ignore-workspace` | ✓ (this is what the `Test: Workflow scripts` CI job runs first) |\n| `npm test --prefix=.github/scripts` | ✓ **436 pass / 0 fail** — the exact command CI runs for this path |\n| `node --test … scripts/mutation-health/mutate.test.mjs` | ✓ 33 pass / 0 fail |\n| Stryker command-runner, exported helpers, changed lines | 83.19% → 88.24% (99→105 killed, 20→14 survived) |\n| Stryker command-runner, all changed lines | 18.43% → 19.82% |\n| `pnpm biome check --write scripts/mutation-health/mutate.test.mjs` | ✓ formatted |\n| `git status` after every `--inPlace` Stryker run | clean — no mutants left behind, no product source modified |\n\nScratch artifacts (`.selfcheck/`, `.stryker-tmp/`, the throwaway Stryker config) were removed; the commit contains only `scripts/mutation-health/mutate.test.mjs`.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- The task asked for `pnpm mutate --diff`. It returned a vacuous green, so rather than report \"all clear\" I scored the same changed lines through a route that works on `.mjs` + `node:test`. The numbers above come from that route, not from `summary.json`.\n- Findings were capped at the top 5 by real reachability, per the brief. The `.test.mts` assertion was folded into the `[cm]?` finding since it is the same rule seen from the exclusion side.\n\n## Related Linear tickets, Github issues, and Community forum posts\n\nAdvisory follow-up on n8n-io/n8n#36746. No ticket of its own.\n\n## Review / Merge checklist\n\n- [x] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\n- [x] PR title and summary are descriptive.\n- [ ] Docs updated or follow-up ticket created. <!-- N/A — test-only change -->\n- [x] Tests included.\n- [ ] PR Labeled with `Backport to Beta`, `Backport to Stable`, or `Backport to v1`\n\n---\n\n*This report was meant to be posted as a PR comment, but `gh pr comment` is outside this run's command allowlist, so it lives in the description instead. Advisory only — not a merge blocker.*\n\n\n---\n🐱 Opened by [cat-bot](https://github.com/n8n-io/cat-bot/actions/runs/32420363199). Review the changes; close if the approach is wrong.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36746/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36430","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36430/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36430/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36430/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36430","id":5171334139,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABAAzkaw","number":36430,"title":"ci: Verify the packed `@n8n/design-system` tarball from a real consumer (no-changelog)","user":{"login":"alexgrozav","id":6179477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzk0Nzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6179477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav","html_url":"https://github.com/alexgrozav","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"alexgrozav","id":6179477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzk0Nzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6179477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav","html_url":"https://github.com/alexgrozav","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-08-17T11:27:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T11:59:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"alexgrozav","id":6179477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzk0Nzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6179477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav","html_url":"https://github.com/alexgrozav","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/36430","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36430","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36430.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36430.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\n`@n8n/design-system` published a broken artifact for months with a green pipeline. Nothing in the monorepo consumed `dist`: every internal package aliases `@n8n/design-system(.*)` to `src$1`, so the published output was never exercised by anything. [N8N-110](https://linear.app/n8n/issue/CAT-3974) fixed the artifact. It did not fix the reason the artifact was allowed to rot.\n\nThis adds the consumer that does exercise it. A new `Packed consumer` required check packs the package, installs the tarball **outside the workspace resolution graph**, then builds, typechecks and loads a generated consumer against it.\n\nhttps://linear.app/n8n/issue/CAT-3981\n\n## What the check does\n\nEach phase fails the job.\n\n1. **Export targets present** — every non-wildcard `exports` target resolves to a file in the tarball.\n2. **Specifier coverage** — every `@n8n/design-system…` specifier written anywhere in the monorepo resolves through the published `exports` map. This catches a deep import that resolves fine inside the workspace through the alias and resolves nowhere for anybody else.\n3. **Peer ranges** — every peer the packed manifest declares matches the range the consumer installs.\n4. **Typecheck** — `vue-tsc --noEmit` over a consumer using `N8nDataTableServer`'s generically typed `#item` slot, whose payload reaches a `@tanstack/vue-table` type through the emitted declarations, plus explicit assertions that the published types have not degraded to `any`.\n5. **Build** — `vite build` with the stock Vue plugin and nothing else. Needing the icon plugin here would mean the pre-built icon chunks stopped shipping.\n6. **Load under plain Node** — each module subpath imported one at a time as native ESM, then an icon body fetched through the public loader for every chunk the icon entry references.\n\nNothing is enumerated by hand. The probe surface comes from the `exports` map, the specifier set from a scan of the repo, the toolchain versions from the target's own manifest via the pnpm catalog, and the expected icon chunks from the icon entry's own dynamic imports. A subpath, consumer or chunk added tomorrow is covered with no edit.\n\nFull rationale, including why `skipLibCheck` stays on and why `--legacy-peer-deps` is not used: `packages/testing/code-health/src/packed-consumer/README.md`.\n\n## Negative controls\n\nA probe not shown to fail on the defect it claims absent is not evidence. Each was injected locally and each failed the job:\n\n| Injected defect | Caught by |\n| --- | --- |\n| `./icons/lucide` removed from the `exports` map | phase 2, naming the importing file |\n| One pre-built icon bucket chunk deleted from `dist` | phase 6, naming the chunk; also phase 5 |\n| `TableHeader<T>` widened to `any` in the shipped `.d.ts` | phase 4 (`TS2344`, plus `TS2578` on the now-unused `@ts-expect-error`) |\n\nThe first version of the chunk probe derived its expectations from a directory listing and therefore passed when a chunk was deleted. It now reads the entry's own dynamic imports.\n\n## Also in this PR\n\nThe check flagged one real deep import surviving on master: `editor-ui/src/features/agents/channels/types.ts` imported `IconName` from `@n8n/design-system/components/N8nIcon/icons`, which is outside the `exports` map. Migrated to the root import — the type is already re-exported from the barrel. This is the class of regression [N8N-128](https://linear.app/n8n/issue/CAT-3976)/[N8N-184](https://linear.app/n8n/issue/CAT-4093) migrated 119 imports for, arriving again with nothing watching.\n\n`loadWorkspace` / `closureOf` / the pack loop moved from `verify-npm-install.ts` to `utils/pack-workspace.ts`, shared by both verifiers. No behaviour change; its existing tests cover it.\n\n## Cost and wiring\n\n- Full run: **~35s** locally (pack, npm install, typecheck, build, load).\n- Gated on the broad `ci` filter rather than a path filter over the package's build config and `exports` map. Half of what this catches is a specifier added elsewhere in the monorepo, and a path filter listing the packages that consume the design system is exactly the hand-maintained list that let the artifact rot in the first place.\n- Added to `required-checks` on PRs, and to `ci-master.yml` — a tarball can break from a dependency resolving differently on master than it did on the branch.\n- A `--static-only` scope runs phases 1–3 in ~6s, for local iteration.\n\n## Review notes\n\n- `test-packed-consumer-reusable.yml` rejects an unknown `scope` rather than defaulting, so a typo cannot silently downgrade the job to the cheap half and leave a green check that compiled nothing.\n- The generated fixture names one component (`N8nDataTableServer`). The acceptance criteria call for a typed slot, which is inherently a named example; if it leaves the barrel the fixture stops compiling, which is a loud failure rather than silent rot.\n- Test files and `packages/testing/code-health/**` are excluded from the specifier scan — both were observed producing phantom findings, since both hold specifiers as fixture data.\n- The `@n8n/chat` fresh-clone `vitest run` confusion from the issue thread is documented in the README (verified locally: `Failed to resolve import \"@n8n/design-system\"`, 2 test files failing, because `dist` is gitignored). Not fixed here — it is a developer-experience issue, not a packaging defect.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36430?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Review round 1 — blocker fixed at the root\n\n@filter found that the specifier scan ran `fast-glob` with the default `dot: false`, so `.storybook/` was never read. Two real violations hid under it, both in `.storybook/preview.ts`: `@n8n/design-system/plugin` and `@n8n/design-system/composables/useIconBodyLoader`, neither in the `exports` map. Reproduced exactly — 16 specifiers instead of 14, both reported.\n\nRather than adding `dot: true`, the scan now enumerates from **`git ls-files`**. That fixes the root cause and closes a second hole found while confirming the first: `storybook-static/` build output was being scanned and contributed four specifiers out of bundled asset chunks. Generated output is never tracked and a dot-directory is tracked like anything else, so neither needs a hand-written exclusion — which was @filter's actual objection. The command throws rather than falling back to a filesystem walk, since a fallback would scan a different set than it reports.\n\n`isScannableFile` and `trackedScannableFiles` are unit-tested, including the dot-directory case and the generated-output case (8 new tests).\n\n### The two `.storybook` imports are grandfathered, not migrated\n\nThe suggested fix was the same one-line root import used for `channels/types.ts`. That would regress a documented property, so it is not applied:\n\n- The deep imports are deliberate. `preview.ts:1-3` states it: `preview.ts` is a TurboSnap global, and the barrel's `export * from './components'` would make every component a global dep, forcing a full Chromatic snapshot on any component change.\n- `git blame` dates them to `8ce1fdca557` (2026-07-27), three weeks before the exports flip (`35bb514616`, today). N8N-184's subpath migration missed them under the same dot-directory blind spot.\n- Both symbols are on the root barrel, so a root import compiles. It just spends Chromatic snapshot budget, and I have no measurement to price that with — so it is not this job's call.\n- Storybook is `private: true` and resolves the package through its own alias to `src` (`storybook/vite.config.ts:38`), so nothing published is at risk. Verified: `pnpm --filter @n8n/storybook build` exits 0, while `import.meta.resolve` of both specifiers fails with `ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED`.\n\nThey sit in `grandfathered.ts` with their reason and are **printed on every run**. The check fails if one becomes resolvable, so the exception cannot outlive its cause, and anything new is enforced normally. This follows the pattern `endpoint-scope-coverage` already uses in this package for pre-existing violations.\n\nThe real resolution is to give `./plugin` its own published entry, exactly as `./icons/lucide` got one — a plugin that pulls the whole component set is the optional capability the barrel should not carry. That needs a build entry as well: `dist/plugin.d.ts` ships today with no `dist/plugin.js`. That expands the published API surface that stage 5 deliberately scoped to six keys, so it is routed to the design-system owner rather than decided here.\n\n### Two new negative controls\n\n| Injected defect | Caught by |\n| --- | --- |\n| A new unexported deep import added to `editor-ui` | phase 2 — the grandfathered list does not excuse it |\n| `./plugin` added to `exports`, making a grandfathered entry stale | phase 2, naming the entry to delete |\n\n### Nits\n\n- **Taken:** the job now gates on `ci == 'true' || workflows == 'true'`. `ci` excludes `.github/**`, so a PR editing only this job's workflow would have skipped it, and `required-checks` passes on a skip.\n- **Taken:** corrected the comment that described `static`/`full` scope wiring no caller uses.\n- **Left:** branch name.\n\nFull gate green in **22s** locally. 161 unit tests pass; lint, biome, prettier and typecheck clean.\n\n\n---\n\n## Closed — not merged\n\nOperator decision, 2026-08-17: a manual consumability check is enough; this gate is not wanted in CI.\n\nClosing rather than reworking. The one real defect this branch found — a deep `@n8n/design-system/components/N8nIcon/icons` import in `editor-ui`, outside the six-key `exports` map — lands separately, together with a by-hand version of the procedure so the check stays repeatable without CI.\n\nBranch `cat-3981-ci-consumes-packed-design-system-tarball` is left in place at `ce70a91838` for reference: the verifier, its 161 tests and the five fault injections are all there if the decision is ever revisited.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36430/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36430/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36719","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36719/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36719/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36719/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36719","id":5202695646,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABAZ-mNw","number":36719,"title":"feat(core): Export git connection projects to repository folder (no-changelog)","user":{"login":"ireneea","id":20843309,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODQzMzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20843309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea","html_url":"https://github.com/ireneea","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ireneea/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1417801476,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE3ODAxNDc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/core","name":"core","color":"DC143C","default":false,"description":"Enhancement outside /nodes-base and /editor-ui"},{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-08-20T11:06:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T14:36:33Z","closed_at":"2026-08-21T14:36:30Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/36719","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36719","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36719.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/36719.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-21T14:36:30Z"},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\n[Demo video](https://www.loom.com/share/cbc3e8ab2a554cea9c0131f64dac09cd)\r\n\r\nAdds a \"push\" operation to Git connections that exports all linked projects into the connection's local working copy — the first half of a full Git sync (committing and pushing to the remote is a follow-up).\r\n\r\n**What's new:**\r\n- **`DirectoryPackageWriter`** — writes the n8n-packages export as loose files (the \"unzipped\" layout) instead of a tar archive.\r\n- **`N8nPackagesService.exportPackageToDirectory`** — uses the new writer and now emits per-resource export counts.\r\n- **`GitConnectionsService.push()`** — exports linked projects into the connection's `repository/n8n-export` subfolder, replacing the previous export wholesale so unlinked projects disappear, while leaving `.git` and any user-committed root files untouched.\r\n- **Public API + CLI** — a new `pushGitConnectionProjects` endpoint (gated by a `gitConnection:push` scope, returns export counts) and a `git-connections push <id>` command.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> Marked `no-changelog`: this exports to the local working copy only. It does not yet commit or push to the remote.\r\n\r\n## How to test\r\n\r\n1. Create a Git connection with one or more linked projects.\r\n2. Run the CLI command `n8n git-connections push <connectionId>` (or call the public API endpoint `pushGitConnectionProjects`).\r\n3. Verify the exported workflows, credentials, variables, and tags appear as loose files under the connection's working copy in `repository/n8n-export`, and that the response returns per-resource export counts.\r\n4. Re-run with a project unlinked and confirm its files are removed from the export folder while `.git` and root files remain untouched.\r\n\r\n## Related Linear tickets, Github issues, and Community forum posts\r\n\r\nhttps://linear.app/n8n/issue/LIGO-966\r\n\r\n## Review / Merge checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\r\n- [x] PR title and summary are descriptive. ([conventions](../blob/master/.github/pull_request_title_conventions.md))\r\n- [ ] [Docs updated](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs) or follow-up ticket created.\r\n- [x] Tests included.\r\n- [x] PR Labeled with `Backport to Beta`, `Backport to Stable`, or `Backport to v1` (if the PR is an urgent fix that needs to be backported)\r\n\r\n🤖 PR Summary generated by AI","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/36719/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}